NAME
  dpkg-deb - build and inspect Freax package archives

SYNOPSIS
  dpkg-deb -b DIR [OUT.fpkg]
  dpkg-deb -c PACKAGE.fpkg
  dpkg-deb -I PACKAGE.fpkg
  dpkg-deb -x PACKAGE.fpkg DIR
  dpkg-deb -e PACKAGE.fpkg DIR

DESCRIPTION
  dpkg-deb works with .fpkg archives, Freax's uncompressed package
  format. An archive begins with the magic line FREAXPKG 1 and ends with
  @end. It holds a control entry, optional maintainer scripts, and one
  entry per installed path: regular files, conffiles, directories, and
  symlinks. There is no compression and no checksum inside the archive;
  repository indexes carry the SHA256 of the whole file (see
  `man apt-ftparchive`).

  For a build directory DIR, dpkg-deb reads DIR/DEBIAN/control and the
  optional scripts DIR/DEBIAN/preinst, postinst, prerm, postrm, and the
  optional list DEBIAN/conffiles (absolute paths that should be treated
  as conffiles). Every other path under DIR becomes a data entry rooted
  at /, so DIR/bin/tool installs to /bin/tool.

  On a successful build, dpkg-deb prints the archive's SHA256 and size.
  Repository tooling uses these values in Packages stanzas.

COMMANDS
  -b, --build DIR [OUT.fpkg]
    Build an archive from DIR. If OUT is omitted the archive is written
    in the current directory as <package>_<version>_all.fpkg, using the
    Package and Version fields from control.
  -c, --contents PACKAGE.fpkg
    List the archive's entries and their paths.
  -I, --info PACKAGE.fpkg
    Print the control fields and any maintainer scripts in the archive.
  -x, --extract PACKAGE.fpkg DIR
    Extract the package's data files into DIR.
  -e, --control PACKAGE.fpkg DIR
    Extract the package's control files and scripts into DIR.

FILES
  DIR/DEBIAN/control
  DIR/DEBIAN/preinst
  DIR/DEBIAN/postinst
  DIR/DEBIAN/prerm
  DIR/DEBIAN/postrm
  DIR/DEBIAN/conffiles

EXAMPLES
  dpkg-deb -b hello
    Build hello_1.0_all.fpkg from the hello directory.

  dpkg-deb -I hello_1.0_all.fpkg
    Show the control fields of the built package.

  dpkg-deb -c hello_1.0_all.fpkg
    List everything the package would install.

  dpkg-deb -x hello_1.0_all.fpkg /tmp/hello
    Unpack the data files for inspection.